{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:joint-critical-clt",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Under the stated four-sample design, \\(\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal F_s}d_{\\mathrm{BL}}(\\mathcal L_P[\\sqrt{n/L_n}(\\widehat\\tau-\\tau(P))],N(0,V(P)))\\to0\\). Uniform map consistency and ass:lift-regularity imply that the half-open-cell lift branch is selected for both \\(\\widehat p\\) and \\(\\widehat T\\) with probability \\(1-o(1)\\), uniformly over \\(\\mathcal F_s\\); hence the measurable fallback has probability \\(o(1)\\) and does not alter the limit. This strictly extends the uniform-to-uniform, fixed-source dimension-two conclusion of Proposition 29 in ManoleBalakrishnanNilesWeedWasserman2023CLT to general variable coefficients and to the four-input nested causal functional.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal F_s\\)",
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(L_n\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat\\tau\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat p\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat T\\)",
      "\\(\\tau(P)\\)",
      "\\(V(P)\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:cell-ratios",
      "ass:cic-identification",
      "ass:density-positivity",
      "ass:density-smoothness",
      "ass:fixed-separated-grid",
      "ass:lift-regularity",
      "ass:four-sample-design",
      "ass:kernel-mass",
      "ass:kernel-order",
      "ass:kernel-symmetry",
      "ass:polynomial-bandwidth",
